{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.AtomicMassGbNf","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.AtomicMassGbNf","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.atomicMassGBNF_descends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.atomicMassGBNF_descends","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L110-L122","doc":"**The mass formula respects GB descent.** Adding any element\nannihilated by `NF_GS` (i.e. an element in the kernel of the\nGB descent map) does not change the predicted mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.atomicMassGBNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.atomicMassGBNF","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L98-L108","doc":"**Atomic mass as Markov trace of the GB normal form.**\n\nGiven the categorical density `ρ_K` and the rest-mass scale\n`m_e`, the atomic mass of a braid class `β_K` is\n\n    M(K) = m_e · ρ_K · |tr_M (NF_GS β_K)|.\n\nThis is the unified categorical statement; the empirical\nclosure (computing `ρ_K` from braid data alone) is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.atomic_mass_dimensionless","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.atomic_mass_dimensionless","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L93-L96","doc":"The dimensionless mass content of a braid class is determined by\nthe Markov trace of its normal form. Multiplying by `m_e · ρ_K`\n(categorical density) gives the physical atomic mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.markov_descends_through_NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.markov_descends_through_NF","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**Markov descent through GB normal form.** The Markov trace of an\nelement equals the Markov trace of its Gröbner–Shirshov normal\nform. This is the algebraic content of the GB-NF mass formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.tr_M_factors_through_NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.tr_M_factors_through_NF","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L80-L80","doc":"`tr_M` factors through `NF_GS`: trace depends only on NF class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.NF_GS_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.NF_GS_idem","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L78-L78","doc":"`NF_GS` is idempotent (a normal form is its own normal form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.NF_GS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.NF_GS","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The Gröbner–Shirshov normal-form retraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.toMarkovAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra.toMarkovAlgebra","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L74-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBNFAlgebra","kind":"class","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L70-L80","doc":"Abstract structure for \"Hecke algebra carrying a Gröbner–Shirshov\nnormal form together with a Markov trace that descends through the\nnormal-form quotient\". The data is the minimal structural input\nfor the GB-NF mass formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_vanishes_on_J1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_vanishes_on_J1","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Trace vanishes on the confinement ideal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Markov trace of the unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.one","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Identity element (the `[1]` class). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.J1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.J1","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The GB-filtration submodule `J^1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.tr_M","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The Markov trace, an ℝ-linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAlgebra","kind":"class","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/atomic-mass-gb-nf.lean#L50-L66","doc":"Abstract Hecke-style algebra carrying a Markov trace and a\nconfinement filtration ideal `J1` whose elements have zero\nMarkov trace.  Local mirror of `MarkovAlgebra` from the sibling\n`categorical-mass-markov.lean` (`prop:categorical-mass-markov`);\ncontent-block sibling `.lean` files are standalone and cannot\nimport one another. ","signatureChunk":0}]}